{"kind":"request","text":"\nCodex: independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of exact head\ne66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297 on request/oversized-attachment-disposition (pushed), worktree\n/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/oversized-attachment-disposition. Governing request 59154b87\n(#22093, the remaining oversized-attachment outcome of #137) under my promise c2c18651, delivering the\nnarrowing of decision fcb32a61 (#5075) that Hugh adopted in proposal ddaf3197 (#22135, ratify ecc3db6f).\nThe reporting artifact is the internal/kernel/kernel.go artifact 4243728e3cfdac5485f526d868c49aa5074f242e, the newest artifact on that promise; it\ncarries the implementation report and the answers to the planner's review acf2c640 (#22166), the adoption\nreconciliation 68e00316 and the independent census 0a048f5d. Thirteen companion artifacts cover the other\nthirteen changed paths at this same head: internal/app/app.go, internal/intent/intent.go,\ninternal/kernel/kernel_test.go, internal/kernel/request_size_test.go, internal/app/sign_ceiling_test.go,\ncmd/gs/main_test.go, cmd/gs/oversized_evidence_test.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/oversized_evidence_test.go,\ninternal/service/oversized_evidence_test.go, notes/2026-08-05-gitseq-design.md,\ndocs/reference/gs/verify.md, docs/reference/limits.md and docs/reference/architecture.md. Fourteen paths,\nfourteen artifacts, all at this exact head; git diff --stat d1ae6ade..HEAD is 1,107 insertions and 28\ndeletions.\n\nThe head is deliberately two commits over base d1ae6ade, and the shape matters to the review. 84289545 is\nthe code and test checkpoint; e66a2977 adds the documents. Three behaviour source basis artifacts were\npublished at 84289545 (kernel e7bd0c2e, app 865529c7, intent cc1d53e5) so the three reference pages can\ncite them by id in their front matter, which is how those pages flare when the behaviour they describe\nmoves. Those three are live predecessors of the kernel.go, app.go and intent.go artifacts at this head and\nare succeeded by them. git merge-tree onto current main 411681f1 is clean (tree bc907edc), and equally\nclean onto c8c29c69, which 411681f1 descends from; none of the fourteen paths changed between those two\nmains.\n\nWhat the change is. The adopted narrowing keeps the hard genesis ceiling and buys two things: a refusal\nthat tells the author what to do, and a refusal that arrives before a signature is spent. The kernel's\naccounting is refactored into one measurement (measureRequest, over the envelope, payload and every\nattachment) and one judgement (requestSize.judge, spending the ceiling as a remaining budget), with\nsaturating addition; the same requests are refused as before, pinned against the replaced stepwise\naccounting kept verbatim as an oracle. The bare \"event exceeds genesis ceiling\" keeps that exact prefix and\ngains the measured total, the ceiling, the envelope/payload/attachment split with the largest attachment\nnamed, and the remedy. New exported kernel.ValidateUnsignedRequestSize runs that same measurement over a\nplaceholder-signed envelope, so an act can be judged before it is signed with one formula rather than two.\ninternal/app signRequest, the only place a submission is signed, encodes the intent, measures those exact\nbytes when the workroom's local record carries a ceiling, refuses before intent.Sign, and otherwise signs\nthe same bytes through new intent.SignEncoded via a Workspace.sign helper that records the signature\nmeasurement inside itself. Because that is the one signing site, the three per-surface preflights my\nearlier candidate added are gone: cmd/gs/main.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and internal/service/ui.go are\nbyte for byte identical to d1ae6ade at this head.\n\nPlease check, at least:\n\n1. Measured equals signed. TestUnsignedMeasurementEqualsTheSignedMeasurement compares the placeholder\n   measurement against the real signed measurement on the verdict and on the refusal text, at the exact\n   ceiling and one byte under, over four boundary shapes. Satisfy yourself that this really is one formula\n   and not a second one that happens to agree on the cases chosen.\n2. Placeholder signature length. The argument rests on the actor key and the signature being fixed widths\n   (32 and 64 bytes) in the envelope. Check intent.Envelope and the encoding to confirm a 64-zero-byte\n   placeholder produces a byte-identical envelope length to a real signature, and that the key-length guard\n   in ValidateUnsignedRequestSize is the right guard.\n3. Saturation. addSize saturates rather than wrapping, judge refuses a saturated measurement outright, and\n   total() saturates so an impossible total reads as enormous rather than small. Check the arithmetic\n   cannot be made to wrap, and that the saturated flag is not merely decorative.\n4. Name bounding. boundedName cuts an attachment name to 128 bytes before it enters an error string,\n   because the kernel measures before the payload tree writer validates names. Check the bound is applied\n   on every path into the diagnostic and that truncation cannot itself mislead.\n5. Refusal before any signature, via the observer. The claim is not \"the error came back first\" but \"no\n   signature was produced\". internal/app records observe.Measurement{OperationSubmit, PathSignature} inside\n   the sign helper, and the tests count it. Check that seam: is there any path that signs without going\n   through Workspace.sign, and is the counter a real observation rather than one that reads zero for the\n   wrong reason (each test proves the counter reaches one on the admitted act).\n6. Zero-ceiling guard. The pre-signing check runs only when w.config.PayloadCeiling \u003e 0, so a read-only\n   attachment or a configuration written before the field existed still signs and acts, with the kernel\n   enforcing the ceiling at admission. Check this cannot be turned into either a bypass or a workroom-wide\n   refusal.\n7. No preflight left in the three surfaces. Confirm cmd/gs/main.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and\n   internal/service/ui.go are unchanged from d1ae6ade at this head, and that gs batch and merge planning\n   still preflight as they did.\n8. The architecture contract paragraph. docs/reference/architecture.md gains \"Size is measured before the\n   signature\" under request authoring, plus the kernel bounds bullet extension. This is the contract change\n   for the application layer and it lands in the same head as the behaviour. Say whether the paragraph\n   states the contract accurately, including the retry-key sentence and the no-local-ceiling sentence.\n9. limits.md census attribution and framing. The figures are the planner's independent census, attributed\n   to assert 0a048f5d and dated. The earlier zero-refusal claim and the five-week headroom-loss claim are\n   withdrawn, the rooms are kept distinct (Gitseq 5.34 times, Tailapp 1.96 times), and the page states what\n   a measurement of accepted records cannot say. Check the numbers against 0a048f5d and check the page does\n   not creep back toward demand evidence. Note the page's one deliberate exception to \"everything here is a\n   refusal\", the dated headroom measurement, and say whether that exception is stated clearly enough.\n\nEvidence attached. evidence/gates-commit1.txt: gates on the tree that became 84289545. gofmt, vet, build,\ndiff --check, the six affected packages and race on kernel/app/service are all rc 0. Two runs came back\nred and both are recorded with their explanation. The internal/docset package run failed once with \"refuse\nverified frontier rollback: depth 22331 is shorter than previously verified depth 22332\", which is\nconcurrent appends to this live workroom moving the local frontier marker under a verified read; the\nimmediate rerun passed and internal/docset was green inside the whole-module run. The whole-module run\nfailed on TestBatchProcessReadsItsFileAndReportsFailures/positional file, a pre-existing progress-line\ntiming sensitivity in cmd/gs/main.go, a file this head does not touch at all; the isolated ./cmd/gs/ rerun\npassed. Both are on commit 1 only. evidence/gates-commit2.txt: gates on the tree that became this head, gofmt,\nvet, build, diff --check, docset and the whole module go test -count=1 ./... all rc 0 with no failures.\nevidence/mutants.txt: thirteen guards neutralised one at a time in a scratch copy outside the repository,\nevery final outcome red. Two survived first time and were fixed rather than argued away, and both\nsurvivals are recorded in the file with their fixes: the saturation clause survived because the\nremaining-budget arithmetic already refused every case the oracle table then held, so the table gained a\nsaturating total against a wholly unspent maximum ceiling; and moving the check behind the signature\nsurvived because the measurement was recorded beside the signing call rather than inside it, so the record\nwas skipped along with the check, which is why the record moved inside Workspace.sign. Every \"signing check\nremoved\" run in the file was repeated after that seam moved, so each recorded outcome is against the\ndelivered source. Please treat the two survivals as the interesting part of that file.\n\nNo genesis change, migration, external storage, automatic URL access, key operation, resident restart or\ndeployment is in this head, and no UI source changes so the embed is unchanged. Record the verdict with\ngs review naming the kernel.go artifact first. I will ratify the verdict, publish any correction on this\nsame commitment, then merge with exact-path succession over the live predecessors, push, confirm green main\nCI and delete the worktree and branch.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4243728e3cfdac5485f526d868c49aa5074f242e","conditions":"DRAFT body.conditions for the #22093 review request (one string, no newlines when filed).\n\nIndependent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of exact head e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297 on request/oversized-attachment-disposition (two commits over base d1ae6ade: 84289545 code and tests, e66a2977 documents; fourteen changed paths, fourteen artifacts at that head), reporting artifact the internal/kernel/kernel.go artifact, newest on promise c2c18651 under request 59154b87 (#22093), delivering the narrowing Hugh adopted in proposal ddaf3197 (ratify ecc3db6f) and answering planner review acf2c640 (#22166), reconciliation 68e00316 and census 0a048f5d. Report approved or changes-requested with gs review naming that artifact first, checking: the placeholder-signed measurement is the same measurement as the signed one, on verdict and refusal text, at the ceiling and one byte under; the fixed 32 and 64 byte key and signature widths that make the placeholder envelope byte-identical, and the actor key length guard; saturating addition that cannot wrap and a saturated measurement refused outright; the 128 byte bound on an untrusted attachment name on every path into the diagnostic; refusal before any signature exists, observed by the signature measurement recorded inside Workspace.sign, with no signing path bypassing that seam and the counter proven to reach one on an admitted act; the zero-ceiling guard being neither a bypass nor a workroom-wide refusal; cmd/gs/main.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and internal/service/ui.go byte-identical to d1ae6ade with no per-surface preflight left and batch and merge planning unchanged; the architecture.md contract paragraph landing in the same head as the behaviour and stating the contract accurately; and limits.md carrying the planner's census attributed to 0a048f5d with the zero-refusal and five-week headroom claims withdrawn and the rooms kept distinct. Evidence: gates-commit1.txt with its two explained transients, gates-commit2.txt all rc 0, and mutants.txt with thirteen guards red including the two recorded survivals and their fixes.","head":"e66a29775d7